  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A conducting wire of parabolic shape, initially <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> is moving with velocity <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> in a non-uniform magnetic field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo></math> as shown in figure. If <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></math> are positive constants and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi></math> is the potential difference developed between the ends of the wire, then the correct statement(s) is/are:<br ><img src=\"assets\\qt0010_a8eb03f745fd.png\"/></p>"
